window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-c6f66ad64ae016bd"]={"key":"ny_main-c6f66ad64ae016bd","group":"ny_main","uid":"c6f66ad64ae016bd","rank":64,"title":"everstead controlled leasing assessment 001","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are a Real Estate Broker at Everstead Council. Ravi Yablonski is waiting this week for a controlled sales proposal for Gallowspring Institute about leasing a six-unit commercial property, and Magda Bergqvist needs it packaged clearly enough for the client to decide whether the opportunity is worth pursuing. The attached `everstead_leasing_control_packet.xlsx` contains the current broker-pipeline extract, the supplied control text, and a draft note; Ivo Chidozie, Jasmin Mbeki, and Maude Seaborne appear in the records. The pipeline uses “qualified tenant” inconsistently: some entries appear to use it for commercial interest, while others use it for completed financial screening. The draft also treats confidential applicant income information as persuasive material for the client, which needs to be dealt with rather than repeated. Prepare `gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf` and write it into the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename. Keep it to no more than three pages and make it suitable to send externally: concise, specific, and understandable without access to your working notes. Test the leasing claims against the controls and the usable evidence in the packet, cleanly distinguish verified facts from bounded assumptions and unresolved gaps, and make the treatment of duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, and differently labelled entries visible enough for the reader to follow the result. Make one clear recommendation about the defensible meaning and use of “qualified tenant” in this proposal, anchored in the cleaned record counts; if the same figure appears in more than one place, it must agree. Do not invent rent, occupancy, screening, or other financial figures, and do not include applicant income or other restricted financial particulars. Do not recommend that Gallowspring Institute sign, proceed, reject, or take any other leasing action—the proposal should support that decision without making it for the client. The controls use both must and should language, and the boundary between a mandatory evidentiary condition and a useful but nonessential corroboration is not obvious from the inconsistent pipeline labels, so state the conclusion you can defend from the supplied packet and finish on that decision rather than on a list of next steps.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/everstead_leasing_control_packet.xlsx` — The single supplied source packet for the assessment: it contains the current leasing-pipeline records, control requirements for external claims and restricted applicant information, and the draft material that needs to be evaluated.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf` — A controlled, client-facing leasing sales proposal that evaluates the supplied leasing claims against the supplied controls and evidence, and gives one bounded recommendation about how the term “qualified tenant” should be used. (Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.; Use exactly the specified filename.; No more than three pages.; Suitable for external client review.; Exclude applicant income and other restricted financial particulars.; Do not recommend whether the client should proceed with, reject, or execute the lease.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/everstead_leasing_control_packet.xlsx","bytes":8444,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/8660cb44950aca0130082d4c0c2fb8294a21770a9c346a639f46d84d361d0910.xlsx","sha256":"8660cb44950aca0130082d4c0c2fb8294a21770a9c346a639f46d84d361d0910","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Leasing packet","row_count":29,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Everstead Council | Leasing Pipeline Control Packet"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Snapshot / as-of: 14 August 2026, 16:40 UTC"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Assessment scope: Gallowspring Institute | six-unit commercial property"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Current leasing pipeline extract"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Record ID","Inquiry ref","Contact","Property / scope","Record activity","Pipeline label","Commercial-interest evidence","Interest signal date","Screening status","Screening recorded","Corroborating contact","Corroboration date","INTERNAL - restricted financial detail","Broker note"]},{"r":"8","cells":["LP-24101","GS-6U-041","Ivo Chidozie","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46246","Qualified Tenant","Email: still reviewing the six-unit space; asked for viewing times","46246","Not started","","Call log: viewing times reconfirmed","46247","Declared income: $96,000; source document on file","Call logged"]},{"r":"9","cells":["LP-24102","GS-6U-041","Ivo Chidozie","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46246","Qualified Tenant","Email: still reviewing the six-unit space; asked for viewing times","46246","Not started","","Call log: viewing times reconfirmed","46247","Declared income: $96,000; source document on file","Call logged"]},{"r":"10","cells":["LP-24103","GS-6U-042","Jasmin Mbeki","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46242","QUALIFIED - tenant","No dated active-interest entry","","Complete","46242","","","Declared income: $61,500; screening file retained","Prior screening file"]},{"r":"11","cells":["LP-24104","GS-6U-043","Maude Seaborne","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46244","Active interest","Email: confirms active interest in the six-unit property","46244","Complete","46245","Call log: property scope reconfirmed","46246","Declared income: $83,000; screening file retained","Scope confirmed"]},{"r":"12","cells":["LP-24105","GS-6U-044","Ivo Chidozie","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46243","Qualified tenant","Pipeline note: interested","","Pending","","","","Documents not received",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["LP-24106","GS-6U-045","Jasmin Mbeki","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46245","Follow-up","Email: interested in terms for this six-unit property","46245","Pending","","","","Declared income: $71,000; screening awaiting","Follow-up open"]},{"r":"14","cells":["LP-24107","","Maude Seaborne","Gallowspring Institute / 6-unit commercial property","46248","Qualified Tenant","Email: interested","31/09/2026","Complete","46248","","","Declared income: $88,000; screening file retained","Ref not entered"]},{"r":"15","cells":["LP-24108","EC-OTHER-011","Jasmin Mbeki","Everstead Council / other commercial listing","46247","Qualified Tenant","Email: confirms interest in another listing","46247","Complete","46247","Call log: other listing reconfirmed","46247","Declared income: $67,000; screening file retained","Different listing"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Broker-pipeline export captured 14-Aug-2026 16:40 UTC | Internal packet"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Controls supplied for external leasing claims"]},{"r":"20","cells":["Ref","Supplied control text"]},{"r":"21","cells":["C1","The phrase \"qualified tenant\" is not defined by the supplied controls. An external proposal must define the meaning it uses and apply that meaning consistently.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["C2","A claim of current commercial interest must be supported by an explicit, dated interest signal in the relevant pipeline evidence.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["C3","A second corroborating contact or record should be used or noted where available, but the absence of a second corroboration is not, by itself, failure of the dated-interest condition.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["C4","Duplicate entries representing the same underlying inquiry and containing no new evidence are one inquiry for assessment and count purposes.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["C5","Malformed records and records outside the specified property or assessment scope must not be used as affirmative evidence or included in cleaned totals.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"26","cells":["C6","Commercial interest and financial screening are separate attributes. One must not be inferred from the other.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["C7","Underlying applicant financial particulars are restricted and must not appear in an external client-facing proposal. A source-supported screening status or limitation may be stated only as needed and without reproducing the underlying particulars.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"28","cells":["C8","External claims must be traceable to the dated source packet. Unsupported rent, occupancy, credit, income, yield, market, or suitability claims must not be added.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"29","cells":["C9","The broker may make a bounded recommendation about the evidentiary meaning and use of a pipeline label, but the external proposal must not approve, reject, or recommend execution of a lease.","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"32","cells":["Draft client note"]},{"r":"33","cells":["There are five qualified tenants for the six-unit property. Ivo's declared income of $96,000 and Maude's declared income of $83,000 make the opportunity persuasive; Jasmin's completed screening proves current demand."]},{"r":"34","cells":[]},{"r":"35","cells":[]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf","bytes":6939,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/4bf64f7cf15b243142ff4a169597e45dbe593ed8a290f675acfb2fa668aff0d6.pdf","sha256":"4bf64f7cf15b243142ff4a169597e45dbe593ed8a290f675acfb2fa668aff0d6","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":" Controlled Leasing Evidence Proposal\n Prepared by Everstead Council | For Gallowspring Institute | Packet as of 14 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n Purpose and basis\n This external-facing assessment evaluates the leasing evidence in the supplied Everstead Council leasing-pipeline packet for\n Gallowspring Institute's six-unit commercial property. It is limited to that dated packet as of 14 Aug 2026; it does not add market, rent,\n occupancy, or other outside information.\n\n\n        3                                                    2                                                          1\n        Dated commercial-interest signal                     Screening recorded as complete                             Both attributes supported\n        of 5 distinct cleaned inquiries                      of 5 distinct cleaned inquiries                            of 5 distinct cleaned inquiries\n\n\n Definition and control application\n Interpretation selected for this proposal. A qualified tenant means a distinct, cleaned, in-scope inquiry with an explicit, dated\n commercial-interest signal. On that definition, the packet supports 3 qualified tenants out of 5 distinct cleaned inquiries. This choice\n follows the supplied mandatory condition for a current commercial-interest claim and is the limited client-facing claim the packet\n supports.\n Mandatory condition. The supplied controls require the dated interest signal for a current commercial-interest claim. The original\n pipeline label is therefore not used as proof by itself.\n Advisory corroboration. A second contact is present for GS-6U-041 and GS-6U-043. It is not recorded for GS-6U-045; that limits\n corroboration but does not negate its explicit dated interest signal because the supplied control treats a second record as should-level\n support, not a mandatory condition.\n Alternate reading retained, not used as the headline. If the phrase instead meant completed financial screening, the count would be\n 2 of 5 (GS-6U-042 and GS-6U-043). One of those has no dated current-interest signal, so this alternate reading would answer a\n different question.\n\n Cleaned population\n      Reconciliation of the supplied extract                     Rows /                   Treatment\n                                                                 inquiries\n\n      Raw pipeline rows                                          8                        Starting extract population\n\n      Outside the property scope                                 -1                       LP-24108 concerns another commercial listing\n\n      Duplicate row with no new evidence                         -1                       LP-24102 is the same inquiry as LP-24101\n\n      Malformed record                                           -1                       LP-24107 has no inquiry reference and an invalid interest date\n\n      Cleaned assessment population                              5                        Distinct in-scope inquiries; not people or raw pipeline rows\n\n\n Evidence register\n      Inquiry / source               Verified commercial-interest evidence                        Verified screening         Control treatment\n                                                                                                  status\n\n      GS-6U-041                      Yes - email, still reviewing the six-unit space; asked       Not started                Counts once; corroborating call recorded\n      LP-24101, LP-24102             for viewing times (12 Aug 2026)                                                         13 Aug\n\n      GS-6U-042                      No dated active-interest signal recorded                     Complete (8 Aug            Screening does not establish current\n      LP-24103                                                                                    2026)                      interest\n\n      GS-6U-043                      Yes - email, confirms active interest in the six-unit        Complete (11 Aug           Interest and screening are separately\n      LP-24104                       property (10 Aug 2026)                                       2026)                      supported; corroborating call recorded 12\n                                                                                                                             Aug\n\n      GS-6U-044                      No affirmative conclusion - undated pipeline note            Pending                    Unresolved; no positive evidence under\n      LP-24105                       only                                                                                    selected definition\n\n      GS-6U-045                      Yes - email, interested in terms for this six-unit           Pending                    Counts for selected definition; no second\n      LP-24106                       property (11 Aug 2026)                                                                  contact recorded\n\n\n\n\nEverstead Council | Controlled leasing evidence assessment                                                                                                               Page 1\n\f Boundaries and record exceptions\n Verified source facts. LP-24101 and LP-24102 share GS-6U-041 and carry no different usable evidence, so they are one inquiry.\n LP-24107 is excluded because its inquiry reference is absent and its interest-signal date is invalid. LP-24108 is excluded because it is\n for another commercial listing.\n Interpretation. Original labels such as \"Qualified Tenant\" and \"Active interest\" are reconciled to the dated interest and screening fields\n rather than accepted at face value. Commercial interest and completed financial screening remain separate attributes.\n Assumption and unresolved gap. No assumption fills missing dates or statuses. GS-6U-044 has an undated interest note and a\n pending screening status, so it is not affirmative evidence. These source limitations bound the assessment; they are not a finding that\n no leasing opportunity exists.\n Information handling. Restricted applicant financial particulars in the source packet and draft note are omitted. Only the\n screening-status labels needed to distinguish the two attributes are included.\n\n\n       Recommendation                        Use qualified tenant in this proposal only for the 3 distinct cleaned, in-scope inquiries with\n       (evidentiary use only)                explicit dated commercial-interest evidence. Completed financial screening remains a\n                                             separate reported attribute and does not substitute for the mandatory interest condition. This\n                                             is a bounded evidence definition from the supplied packet, not a recommendation that\n                                             Gallowspring Institute take a leasing action.\n\n\n\n\nEverstead Council | Controlled leasing evidence assessment                                                                                    Page 2\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a PDF with the exact filename `gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file path and extension.","grader_hint":"Check the top-level submission path and confirm the filename and PDF MIME/signature. This is a scaffolding item only."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF opens and renders with legible text and no materially missing, clipped, or corrupted content.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF pages.","grader_hint":"Open or render the PDF offline and inspect all pages for readable content, intact tables, and absent rendering failures."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal is no longer than three pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PDF page count.","grader_hint":"Count rendered PDF pages; three pages is compliant."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document reads as an external client-facing proposal rather than internal analyst notes or a raw data dump.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall document voice, framing, and presentation.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a client could read it without knowing the broker's private workflow, while still seeing the relevant evidence limitations."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal correctly identifies Everstead Council, Gallowspring Institute, and the six-unit commercial property, and states that its purpose is to assess the leasing evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Client/context statement in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Confirm all three supplied context elements are present and not confused with applicant or broker records."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal states the applicable snapshot or as-of date and ties its factual claims to the supplied packet rather than presenting them as timeless facts.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"As-of statement and source references in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated date with the dated snapshot in the workbook and check that the proposal signals the temporal scope of its assessment."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment applies only the controls and jurisdictional material supplied in the workbook and does not introduce an unsupported external legal, regulatory, or market requirement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claims, control discussion, and cited basis.","grader_hint":"Look for outside statutes, invented thresholds, or claims of legal compliance not grounded in the supplied control text."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal makes the evidentiary limitations of a single, imperfect pipeline source visible without treating every source defect as proof that no leasing opportunity exists.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations or basis section and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Reward a proportionate limitation statement that distinguishes source reliability problems from the underlying commercial opportunity."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal explicitly identifies the ambiguity between “qualified tenant” as commercial interest and “qualified tenant” as completed financial screening.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition or findings text.","grader_hint":"Both competing meanings must be named or unmistakably described; merely saying that labels are inconsistent is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal chooses one defensible meaning of “qualified tenant” for this proposal and explains why that meaning is appropriate to the evidence and client-facing purpose.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition and rationale.","grader_hint":"Accept either the commercially-interested or financially-screened interpretation if it is deliberate, evidence-compatible, and clearly bounded."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal acknowledges the consequence of the other reasonable interpretation instead of silently treating its chosen definition as the only possible meaning.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definition comparison or limitation text.","grader_hint":"The reader should be able to see how the result would differ if the alternate meaning were used, without requiring a second competing recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every use of “qualified tenant” in the proposal follows the chosen definition, with no switching between commercial-interest and financial-screening meanings.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All occurrences of the term and related conclusions.","grader_hint":"Trace the term through the summary, evidence discussion, tables, and conclusion; inconsistent shorthand fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal contains exactly one clear recommendation, directed to the evidentiary treatment and use of “qualified tenant,” rather than several competing recommendations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and conclusion text.","grader_hint":"Accept one bounded call such as how the label should be used and what the cleaned evidence supports. Do not require a particular chosen meaning."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal does not recommend that Gallowspring Institute proceed, reject the opportunity, sign, execute, or take another leasing action.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation, conclusion, and calls to action.","grader_hint":"A neutral statement that the evidence supports the client's decision is acceptable; an instruction or recommendation about the lease decision is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal ends on the bounded evidentiary decision and does not finish with a generic next-steps list that substitutes for a conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final section or final paragraph.","grader_hint":"The final substantive statement should be the decision or recommendation, not merely an invitation to gather more information."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Verified facts, interpretations, and assumptions are visibly distinguished so that a reader can tell which statements come directly from the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fact/findings presentation throughout the PDF.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit labels, careful wording, or an equivalent structure; a polished narrative that blends source facts with inference does not satisfy this."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal identifies material unresolved gaps or uncertain records and avoids converting them into positive leasing evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations, exceptions, and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Check that missing, malformed, or ambiguous information remains bounded and is reflected in the strength of the conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Duplicate pipeline entries are treated as one underlying inquiry when the packet indicates that they contain no new evidence, and the treatment is explained.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-cleaning explanation and evidence table.","grader_hint":"Compare the proposal's treatment with the repeated inquiry keys and duplicate indicators in the workbook; reward explicit rationale, not a merely reduced total."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal does not count duplicate rows as separate tenants, separate expressions of interest, or separate screening outcomes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Counts and supporting table.","grader_hint":"Recompute the relevant distinct underlying inquiries from the workbook and compare them with the proposal's denominators and totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Malformed records are excluded from affirmative evidence and from the applicable cleaned counts, with the reason for exclusion stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception treatment and counts.","grader_hint":"Identify the malformed entries in the packet and verify that missing or invalid required fields are not silently treated as positive status."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Rows outside the six-unit property's relevant scope or otherwise marked irrelevant are excluded from the assessment population.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope definition and cleaned population.","grader_hint":"Compare included records with the property and relevance fields in the workbook; the proposal should not inflate evidence with unrelated rows."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Inconsistent pipeline labels are reconciled transparently to underlying evidence rather than being accepted at face value or silently overwritten.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Label treatment, mapping explanation, and record-level findings.","grader_hint":"The document should explain how labels were interpreted in light of dated interest and screening fields, while preserving uncertainty where the source cannot resolve it."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any claim of current commercial interest is tied to a dated, explicit interest signal in the supplied records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interest findings and cited records.","grader_hint":"For each affirmative current-interest claim, locate a corresponding dated signal in the workbook; old or inferred interest does not qualify."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal distinguishes the packet's mandatory evidentiary condition from its advisory corroboration guidance instead of treating every useful check as a must-have.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Controls assessment and recommendation.","grader_hint":"Look specifically for the difference between the required dated interest signal and the separate should-level corroboration guidance."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal uses available corroborating evidence where present but does not falsely state that a second corroborating record is mandatory when the supplied controls make it advisory.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Record analysis and control interpretation.","grader_hint":"Verify both sides: corroboration is not ignored, and its absence is not automatically treated as failure of the mandatory current-interest condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Commercial interest and completed financial screening are presented as separate attributes, not as interchangeable evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions, evidence table, and summary.","grader_hint":"The proposal should allow the reader to see the two dimensions independently before applying the selected definition."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal does not infer financial screening completion merely because a record shows commercial interest or a positive pipeline label.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Screening claims and record citations.","grader_hint":"Check every financially framed assertion against the screening-status field or explicit screening evidence in the workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal does not infer current commercial interest merely because a record shows financial screening completion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interest claims and record citations.","grader_hint":"A screening result alone cannot serve as the dated interest signal required by the supplied controls."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF contains no applicant income amounts or other raw restricted financial particulars from the workbook.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full PDF text and rendered pages.","grader_hint":"Search extracted text and inspect rendered pages for income amounts, employer or account details, debt figures, credit scores, or equivalent underlying financial particulars."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Restricted applicant information is minimized: the proposal discusses only the permitted screening status or limitation needed for the client's decision and does not reproduce unnecessary personal detail.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Applicant references and screening discussion.","grader_hint":"Do not penalize necessary synthetic contact references, but reject gratuitous personal financial or identifying detail that is not needed to support the bounded conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any statement that financial screening is complete, pending, or unavailable matches the corresponding supported status in the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Screening-status statements and source records.","grader_hint":"Reconcile each status statement to the supplied status/evidence fields; do not require disclosure of the restricted underlying data."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal does not invent rent, occupancy, credit, income, yield, market, or other financial metrics that are absent from the supplied evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All quantitative and market claims in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Check numerical claims against the workbook. Qualitative statements must not imply unsupported figures."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reported cleaned population and component counts are derived from the in-scope, non-duplicate, non-malformed records rather than raw row totals.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Counts, denominator statement, and data-cleaning explanation.","grader_hint":"Recompute the cleaned population from the packet's record relationships and exclusions; accept regenerated values, not a fixed literal answer."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The count reported as meeting the chosen “qualified tenant” definition equals the number of distinct cleaned records satisfying that definition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Qualified count and supporting evidence.","grader_hint":"Evaluate the count against the definition the proposal itself chose; either permitted interpretation is acceptable if applied consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal defines what its denominators count, including whether counts refer to distinct inquiries, people, or pipeline rows.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Metric definitions or table labels.","grader_hint":"A reader must be able to understand the unit of every reported count without reverse-engineering the workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Repeated numeric conclusions agree across the executive summary, evidence presentation, and final recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All repeated counts in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Identify the principal chosen-definition count and verify that every occurrence uses the same value and unit."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material affirmative and exclusionary claims are traceable to record identifiers or an equivalent source reference in the supplied workbook.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence register, footnotes, or record references.","grader_hint":"Trace representative claims from each category back to the workbook; a generic citation to the file alone is not enough for material record-level claims."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The evidence presentation preserves the relevant date and status distinction for records used to support interest or screening conclusions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence table or narrative citations.","grader_hint":"The reader should be able to tell why a record supports a claim and when that evidence was recorded."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Excluded, malformed, duplicate, or unresolved records are disclosed in a concise way that lets the client understand how the headline result was bounded.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exceptions or methodology summary.","grader_hint":"Reward a compact reconciliation or equivalent explanation; the proposal need not reproduce every raw row."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal uses specific, unambiguous language about interest, screening, qualification, and evidentiary strength, avoiding an unqualified promotional use of “qualified tenant.”","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Wording throughout the PDF.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a client could tell what is known, what the label means, and what the evidence does not establish."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The comparison of source claims with controls gives Gallowspring Institute a meaningful basis for its own proceed-or-not decision without overstating the broker's authority.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary, findings, and conclusion.","grader_hint":"The document should be decision-useful: it should identify what the evidence supports and what it cannot establish, while leaving the leasing action to the client."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A competent external reader can understand the conclusion, its numerical basis, and its principal limitations without asking the author to explain the document.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered PDF.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability, logical flow, concise presentation, and whether the recommendation is unambiguous and self-contained."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is an external-facing compliance assessment in a brokerage workflow where inconsistent pipeline labels and restricted applicant information could make a leasing proposal overstate what the evidence supports. The broker has authority to make a bounded evidentiary recommendation, but not to make the client's leasing decision.","difficulty_sources":["judgment_load=3: the solver must choose and defend one of two reasonable meanings of “qualified tenant” while preserving the alternate reading and the boundary between mandatory evidence and advisory corroboration.","reference_count=1: all factual and control evidence is contained in one imperfect supplied workbook.","transformation_depth=2: the solver must clean, deduplicate, scope, classify, and count the source records before restructuring the result into a client-facing proposal.","The central professional tension is preventing restricted applicant financial information from becoming persuasive external sales evidence while still communicating any permitted screening-status limitation.","The second professional tension is deciding which evidence condition is a must and which corroboration is only a should in the context of inconsistent pipeline labels."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_file":{"filename":"everstead_leasing_control_packet.xlsx","purpose":"Create one offline workbook serving as the complete source packet. It should combine the supplied control text, a dated pipeline snapshot, and the problematic draft note so the solver has one discoverable source.","content_constraints":["Use only the organisations and people named in the task request; all identifiers and financial values must be synthetic.","Include a clear snapshot/as-of date and a property scope identifying the six-unit commercial property without inventing a real address.","Include raw pipeline records with distinct record identifiers and fields sufficient to determine property scope, activity date, commercial-interest evidence, financial-screening status, and the original pipeline label.","Include at least one duplicate pair or duplicate cluster that contains no new evidence and can be recognised as the same underlying inquiry, at least one malformed record with a missing or invalid required field, at least one irrelevant or out-of-scope record, and multiple inconsistent uses of the original “qualified tenant” label.","Ensure the usable records contain all necessary combinations for the ambiguity: at least one underlying inquiry supported as commercially interested but not financially screened, at least one financially screened but lacking a current interest signal, and at least one record supporting both dimensions. Include at least one unresolved or insufficient record.","Include enough source dates and status information for a solver to calculate distinct cleaned counts and to cite representative evidence without relying on hidden facts.","Include restricted applicant financial particulars such as synthetic income data, clearly marked as restricted/internal-use-only. Include a draft note that misuses such information as persuasive sales evidence, so the solver must actively prevent its carry-through.","Do not include a hidden answer key or a required preferred interpretation of “qualified tenant.”"],"control_text":["The phrase “qualified tenant” is not defined by the supplied controls. An external proposal must define the meaning it uses and apply that meaning consistently.","A claim of current commercial interest must be supported by an explicit, dated interest signal in the relevant pipeline evidence.","A second corroborating contact or record should be used or noted where available, but the absence of a second corroboration is not, by itself, failure of the dated-interest condition.","Duplicate entries representing the same underlying inquiry and containing no new evidence are one inquiry for assessment and count purposes.","Malformed records and records outside the specified property or assessment scope must not be used as affirmative evidence or included in cleaned totals.","Commercial interest and financial screening are separate attributes. One must not be inferred from the other.","Underlying applicant financial particulars are restricted and must not appear in an external client-facing proposal. A source-supported screening status or limitation may be stated only as needed and without reproducing the underlying particulars.","External claims must be traceable to the dated source packet. Unsupported rent, occupancy, credit, income, yield, market, or suitability claims must not be added.","The broker may make a bounded recommendation about the evidentiary meaning and use of a pipeline label, but the external proposal must not approve, reject, or recommend execution of a lease."],"gold_derivation":["Identify the in-scope property records from the snapshot, remove the out-of-scope records, remove malformed records from affirmative evidence and totals, and collapse duplicate entries according to the supplied duplicate rule.","From the resulting distinct inquiry set, compute the number with a dated explicit commercial-interest signal, the number with supported completed financial screening, and the number satisfying each of the two possible interpretations of “qualified tenant.”","Do not require one of those interpretations as the answer. A passing reference solution may select either commercial interest or completed financial screening, provided it defines the choice, explains the alternate reading, uses the same choice throughout, and reconciles its counts.","The source should make the two interpretations produce meaningfully different results, so a solver cannot pass by merely repeating the request's ambiguity.","The gold proposal should separate source facts, bounded assumptions, and unresolved gaps; explain duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, and inconsistent-label treatment; apply the must/should distinction; omit all restricted financial particulars; and end with one evidentiary recommendation rather than a leasing action recommendation.","Use relational grading predicates against the generated source relationships instead of embedding fixed cell values or fixed expected counts in the rubric."]},"reference_solution":{"construction_requirements":["Produce a concise, rendered PDF within the three-page cap.","Include an externally understandable context statement, as-of date, source basis, definition choice, cleaned evidence summary, limitations, and one final evidentiary recommendation.","Use record-level references or equivalent citations to make material claims auditable.","Include the principal chosen-definition count consistently wherever repeated, with a clear denominator and unit.","Do not reproduce synthetic income amounts or other restricted financial particulars from the source."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"leasing_control_packet","filename":"everstead_leasing_control_packet.xlsx","purpose":"The single supplied source packet for the assessment: it contains the current leasing-pipeline records, control requirements for external claims and restricted applicant information, and the draft material that needs to be evaluated.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the supplied workbook from the starting working directory; it is the only reference file for this request."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"controlled_leasing_proposal","filename":"gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"A controlled, client-facing leasing sales proposal that evaluates the supplied leasing claims against the supplied controls and evidence, and gives one bounded recommendation about how the term “qualified tenant” should be used.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.","Use exactly the specified filename.","No more than three pages.","Suitable for external client review.","Exclude applicant income and other restricted financial particulars.","Do not recommend whether the client should proceed with, reject, or execute the lease."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Use an independent domain reviewer to assess the professional judgment items and a deterministic offline check for file, page-count, text-presence, arithmetic, source-traceability, and restricted-data conditions. Accept either explicitly defended interpretation of “qualified tenant” where all downstream counts and claims follow it.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The source intentionally permits two defensible meanings of “qualified tenant,” so grading must evaluate consistency and rationale rather than a single literal qualified count.","Visual usability and whether the external tone is genuinely client-ready require rendered-PDF review in addition to text extraction."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:37+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:37+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:37+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:24:37+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/c6f66ad64ae016bd","declared_deliverables":["gallowspring_controlled_leasing_proposal.pdf"]};
